    affiliation: "Delft University of Technology"

abstract: >-
  A time-dependent backward erosion piping (BEP) reliability engine for the
  Tokachi and Satsunai levees near Obihiro, Hokkaido. It quantifies the bias
  between the static Sellmeijer (2011) limit state and the transient Pol (2024)
  limit state by Monte Carlo fragility analysis on a shared sample, updates the
  resulting prior against the observed survival of the 2016 typhoon by
  Accept-Reject Bayesian updating, and composes the result with the other levee
  failure mechanisms into an annualised system reliability per 200 m segment
  under a historical and a +4 K climate scenario. Built as the computational
  evidence base for an MSc thesis in Hydraulic Engineering at Delft University
  of Technology.

keywords:
  - backward erosion piping
  - levee reliability
  - flood risk
  - Sellmeijer
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - Bayesian updating
  - fragility curves
  - climate change
  - Tokachi River

